<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Danish–Hanseatic War (1361–1370)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1361">1361</a>–<a href="/years/1370">1370</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Danish–Hanseatic War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Danish–Hanseatic War of 1361–1370 was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdemar-iv-of-denmark">Valdemar IV of Denmark</a> and the Hanseatic towns after Valdemar captured Visby on Gotland in 1361. After an early Danish victory, the Hanseatic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/confederation-of-cologne">Confederation of Cologne</a> and its allies defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> in a second war from 1367. The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stralsund">Stralsund</a> in 1370 gave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a> extensive trading rights and control of fortresses in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scania">Scania</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/danish-hanseatic-war-1361-1370.jpg" alt="Danish–Hanseatic War (1361–1370)" width="320" height="264" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Statens Arkiver - Danish State Archives · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Valdemar_Atterdag_indtager_Visby_(9291726976).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
